hello i'm dianne bapsky and i serve as  the associate director for library  operations or as we typically call it lo  ello supports the library's dual roles  as a national library and is one of the  27 institutes at the national institutes  of health as a national library we are  responsible for nlm's core functions to  collect preserve and make accessible  biomedical information as one of the  institutes at the nih we support the  nih's mission to foster biomedical  discoveries and innovative research  in all activities we strive to embody  the one nlm concept working together  with our other nlm divisions to support  our collective mission  lo is one of the largest divisions in  nlm  our division includes over 450 federal  and contract staff  interns and volunteers  we have a broad range of subject matter  expertise from library science public  health history of medicine to  terminology and systems  let's move on to vision  responsive to our mission we envision a  future in which data and information  will continue to transform and  accelerate biomedical discovery and  improve health and health care globally  and our values  important to how we operate our core  values our user focus service knowledge  sharing quality and trustworthiness  to succinctly communicate what we do and  why it matters i'd like to introduce  ello's three c's  collect curate and connect  so let's start with our first c collect  we collect by acquiring and maintaining  an international collection from  monographs and manuscripts to serials  and data sets  beyond the physical items in the stacks  our collection includes digital objects  including web archives vocabulary such  as medical subject headings or mesh  full text electronic books digitized  manuscript collections and a data  discovery platform serving bulk and  serialized downloads and apis or  application programming interfaces for  many of our products and services  let's move on to the next c curate  we curate by cataloging indexing  processing and making metadata to make  biomedical information findable and  accessible  and with our final c we connect by  linking our diverse global audience to  nlm products and services for users of  all backgrounds to learn  research and discover information about  health and biomedical matters  ello is also home to nlm's field force  for outreach the network of the national  library of medicine we also host  fellowships for early career librarians  traveling exhibitions to bring nlm  collections to local communities and  other professional and international  partnerships  i hope you learned more about the work  we do in library operations and how your  role contributes to our collective  success  welcome to library operations and  welcome to the national library of  medicine
 

